#93002
"Black Marble Hall - Base of an Incline"
"The hallway slopes steadily upwards to the east, its polished floor finally
leveling out after covering more than twenty feet vertically.  A fresh breeze
blows steadily from above, indicating that an opening in the thick stone of
the mountain lies somewhere in that direction.  The walls and floor are of
solid black marble, polished as smooth as glass, perfectly reflecting both
sound and light.  No seams are evident where walls and floor meet, suggesting
that perhaps this hall was cut directly into marble, rather than lined with
it.  Hanging on a chain overhead is a large white orb, which sheds a sombre
light throughout the hall.
"
