"Intersection of Halls - Portal"
"Here at the intersection of two halls, one of white marble leading north and
south, one of black marble leading east and west, stands a scintillating
elliptical portal on a dais of checkered marble.  The floor matches the dais,
tiled in a checkered pattern of black and white stone.  Overhead, a white orb
hangs on a golden chain, casting a pale white light over the room.  An arched
entranceway leads west, beside which a plaque is placed on a rectangular
column of jet black stone.
"
