"White Marble Hall"
"This is a hall of pure white marble, leading north, south and west.  The walls
and floor are polished smooth and clean, reflecting every movement.  On a
silver chain, a white orb hangs about twelve feet from the ground, casting a
pale light through the room.  The ceiling above is vaulted, and many arches
span the hall.  To the west is what looks like a long barracks, one more
luxurious and beautifully crafted than is typical.  A set of white stone
stairs is visible to the north, leading upwards.  To the south, this hall
intersects with another.
"
