#93019
"Barracks of White Marble"
"Barred slit windows around six feet in height are placed in the wall to the
south, looking out on a black marble hallway.  Between the windows are small
weapon racks with spears, swords, crossbows, and crossbow bolts secured to
them.  A central walkway of clean, polished stone runs between the windows and
the living space to the north, lit from above by mysterious white orbs
suspended from chains on the ceiling.  A trough of running water is set into
the northern wall of the barracks, with comfortable-looking cots neatly lined
up and anchored to the floor in the space between the walkway and the wall.
An arched entranceway leads into a hall to the west, while the barracks
continue to the west.
