#93020
"Barracks of White Marble"
"Swirled white marble makes up the walls, floor, and ceiling of this large,
clean-looking barracks.  Thin, angular windows set with steel bars look out on
a passage to the south, on the floor of which can be seen glowing white runes.
Attached to the stone of the ground itself to the north are neat rows of soft-
looking cots.  Just beyond, cut into the stone of northern wall, is a trough
of clean running water.  White orbs hang from chains on the ceiling, casting a
pale glow which lights the room.  The barracks continue to the east and west.
"
