"Barracks of White Marble"
"A cleared, central walkway runs east and west through the barracks here, lined
by rows of clean, comfortable-looking cots to the north, and the wall to the
south.  Set about knee high in the wall are man-high barred windows, looking
out on a hallway to the south.  Carved into the northern wall is a two-foot
wide trough of clear, moving water which runs the whole length of the
barracks.  It follows the wall to the west, then curves around the corner.
The whole scene is lit from above by pale white orbs suspended from the
ceiling.
"
