#93064
"Barracks of White Marble - Kitchen"
"This area is dominated by rows of stoves and cupboards lined up in the center
of the room, ladles and all manner of other utensils hanging from hooks
suspended above the stoves.  A channel has been carved into the wall to the
east and north, and in it flows clean water.  The trough ends in a black hole
in the wall to the west, where water pours silently into the darkness.  Pit
toilets have been set in a row adjacent to the water trough.  Large dining
tables are placed in a rectangle about the central cooking area, long benches
attached on each side of them.  A large black and white mural covers the whole
western wall, and continues along it to the south, even past the kitchen area.
"
""
