"Beneath a Toilet - Crevasse of Sewage"
"Globs of slime-mold and ancient human filth drip down the slick walls of this
dark crevasse, pooling in the bottom.  The sludge is about two feet deep,
thick as porridge and probably far less tasty.  East to west, the crevasse is
about thirty-five feet long, while its north-south width is only about ten
feet.  Set into the stone of the cavern wall to the north are the rusty iron
rungs of a service ladder, which leads up to a bright hole in the ceiling.
"
